ed metrics of the sealed final evaluation (three evaluation seeds, identical across seeds). Displacement rates are at the 2\\% budget.}\npaper.tex:296:Three seed-level records were produced (seeds 201, 202, 203), each with the identical family-averaged score $0.6057$ and recorded durations of $23.1$, $11.8$ and $11.6$ seconds. % @evidence[[paper_data.json#final_evaluation.evaluation_evidence.episodes]]\npaper.tex:297:The identical scores are expected: the proposer is deterministic, a seed never selects data or workload, and the anonymisation of competitor indices is fixed for each case by the evaluator. Durations vary by a factor of two between records and we do not attribute the difference to any cause. The evaluator labels candidate-produced diagnostics as unverified; none of our statements relies on them, and all quantities are computed by the trusted refit.\npaper.tex:308:The frozen configuration is identical to the starter code of the task (same source tree hash), so the studied method and the evaluator's influence baseline share this logic. % @evidence[[source_evidence/downstream/program/src/program.py#_propose]]\n321 paper.tex\n# Agentic evidence audit feedback\n\n- generated_at: `2026-10-28T21:52:31.847687+00:00`\n- ok: `False`\n- verdict: `fail`\n\n## Repair pass (audit + figure manifest)\n- Removed ungrounded design size / \"six models\" claims (Table 1, competitors bullet); reworded permuted-control claim to the single control run per case; limited Yang2026Preference/Seetharaman2021Influence descriptions to title-supported content; softened Giordano/Holy/Szczecinski descriptions.\n- Concept-figure render failed (rc=1): shipped documented matplotlib fallback (scripts/build_overview.py, PDF+PNG), manifest uses list-valued categories/series_per_panel and generator=matplotlib, attempted_generator=generate-concept-figure.\n- validate_claims passes (14 claims, 30 refs); manifest validates against schema; paper compiles (13 pages incl. refs/SI).","stderr":"","in