\\\ % @evidence[[paper_data.json#final_evaluation.metrics.flip_rate_sports_drop]] @evidence[[paper_data.json#final_evaluation.metrics.flip_rate_sports_flip]]\n202:Panel (b) of Figure~\\ref{fig:scores} compares the studied search with the evaluator's reference policies on the same family-averaged scale. The constant and random policies score $0.071$ each, so, averaged over all cases, a generic perturbation of at most 2\\% of the rows closes only a small frac\n215:The measurement supports the statement that, with this heuristic, within these budgets and on these twelve cases, rank-1 vulnerability decreases in the order crowd, sports, expert human, LLM judge. The ordering is an observation for one attack and one target. Failure to displace rank 1 (LLM judg\n232:In the one design where the two modes differ (expert human), reversal succeeds and dropping does not. This is consistent with property (iii) of Section~\\ref{sec:influence}: for the same rows, reversal has a larger first-order effect than removal by the factor $1/|\\tilde y_i-p_i|$. It remains a s\n241:\\paragraph{Design confounds and few cases.} The four designs are specific datasets, not random draws from design classes; they are confounded with size, number of competitors, margin and tie rate. Three of the four designs have one case per edit mode. The NBA data are game results, not preferenc\n247:We measured, with exact-refit verification, how a one-shot first-order influence search fares at displacing the rank-1 competitor of a ridge Bradley--Terry leaderboard using 0.1\\% to 2\\% of the rows, on crowd, expert-human, LLM-judge and sports data. The family-averaged edit success is 0.606, an\n263:The sealed final evaluation has twelve cases (crowd, expert human and LLM judge: one data source $\\times$ two modes; sports: three seasons $\\times$ two modes), three primary seeds and one permuted control episode per case, with each episode issuing five budget calls. % @evidence[[source_evidence\n279:Edit success: crowd / sports & 1.0000 / 0.8328 \\\\\n281:Displacement, drop: crowd / sports / expert human / LLM judge & 1 / 1 / 0 / 0 \\\\\n282:Displacement, flip: crowd / sports / expert human / LLM judge & 1 / 1 / 1 / 0 \\\\","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
