in text.\"),\n]\nfor a,b in reps:\n    assert a in s, a[:40]\n    s=s.replace(a,b)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\nsed -n 262,266p paper.tex | cut -c1-700; grep -n -i \"identical to the starter\\|same source tree\" paper.tex | cut -c1-80"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1463,"cache_read_input_tokens":48510,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1463,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"67422bf1-0c6e-48c7-8ffa-5e0ce2de1e91","uuid":"df0a4f58-f4a5-4212-8cb6-e8dc72aaea78","timestamp":"2026-10-28T21:52:48.452Z","request_id":"req_011CgVNppzyPbki2Pz9Lmg7N"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014hSwYdXAuq1febLN9TbaSe","type":"tool_result","content":"The evaluation interface is a request--response protocol with a reset operation (clearing all proposer state and seeding it) and a propose operation. Each propose request carries the mode, the budget $k$, the number of competitors, the number of rows and base64-encoded integer arrays of competitor indices and outcomes, with rows in the order of the original data. Each call has a hard wall-clock limit of 30 seconds, and the proposer runs on CPU with two threads. Responses with extra keys, non-integer or duplicate or out-of-range indices, more than $k$ indices, or tie rows in flip mode are invalid and score zero for that level. % @evidence[[source_evidence/downstream/program/src/program.py#han\nThe sealed final evaluation has twelve cases (crowd, expert human and LLM judge: one data source $\\times$ two modes; sports: three seasons $\\times$ two modes), three primary seeds and one permuted control episode per case, with each episode issuing five budget calls. % @evidence[[source_evidence/task/evaluate_final.py#CASE_SPECS]]\nDesign scores average cases within a design; family weights are $0.25$ each. The evaluator computes ranks and gaps from its own Newton fit, and its Newton fitter was cross-checked once against an independent L-BFGS fit on at most the first 600 rows of the smallest case (not on every edited refit or unedited case); the target is judged on the original rank-1 competitor's gap to the best other competitor on the refit of the edited data.\n\n\\subsection{Complete Final Metric Table}\n308:The frozen configuration is identical to the starter code of the task (same","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"67422bf1-0c6e-48c7-8ffa-5e0ce2de1e91","uuid":"a198b0f5-8ad6-4caf-9efa-d510d2a93a9d","timestamp":"2026-10-28T21:52:48.519Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"The evaluation interface is a request--response proto